   518	## 6. Limits of this evidence
   519	
   520	- The proof is prose. A reader checks it lemma by lemma, and nothing has machine-checked it. Lean was judged
   521	  unnecessary: every lemma is a decoder-inverts-encoder argument over a fixed grammar.
   522	- "Two implementations agree" is weaker than independence. Both come from one author instance on one runtime, and
   523	  they share the Unicode tables and float conversion. The V1 build is the registered second encoder (V1-DERIVATION
   524	  §5), and it must reproduce these bytes.
   525	- (N) is assumed, not tested exhaustively. N-01 to N-22 check it against RFC 8785's own Appendix B values.
   526	- The golden fingerprints (K-01 `spki-sha256`, K-02 `gpg-sha256`) use the P-256 points G and 2G, and the spec,
   527	  vector, preamble and snapshot bytes are marked ILLUSTRATIVE. The real values come from the real keys and
   528	  documents at the freeze. The layouts do not change.
   529	- The vector signatures are mathematically real, but their private keys are 1 and 2, so anyone can forge them.
