   430	## 5. Evidence: the vectors, and the two-implementation check
   431	
   432	`vectors/gen.py` is implementation A: standard library plus `rfc8785` 0.1.4 for serialization. `vectors/check.py`
   433	is implementation B: standard library only, with its own UTF-8 decoder, JSON parser, ECMAScript number formatter,
   434	JCS serializer and every decoder. Since 2026-10-12, B also has its own OpenPGP signature-packet parser and its
   435	own ECDSA P-256 verifier. The two share no code. They share only Python's Unicode 16.0.0 tables, `float`/`repr`
   436	and `hashlib`'s SHA-256.
   437	- A also uses `hmac` (RFC 6979 nonces, pinned by RFC 6979 A.2.5) and SHA-1, both only to *make* the vector
   438	  signatures.
   439	- SHA-1 fills OpenPGP's issuer-fingerprint subpacket. No check reads it, and B never computes it.
