prototype/indep-verifier/codex-r4.log:13823:'A03': '| A03 | 3.1, 5.1, 7.1, 9 | Originally no assigned pair id, mode/context or SPKI supplement was available. Which hybrid id is codec-known? | Superseded by the supplied supplement and the profile §8 registry owner decision: every installation knows the classical baseline; only an installed catalog selecting the exact hybrid pair registers its codec. Other well-formed ids, including the pair under fallback, remain opaque. The catalog selects semantic support independently of bundle spec lookup. No dated registration is asserted; see A14. | "'`codec.py:registered_codecs`, `signature_rule`; `verify.py:verify_bundle`; profile §8 Codec registry per installation; supplement §§1–3 |'"',
prototype/indep-verifier/codex-r4.log:13824:'A14': '| A14 | 3.1, 7.1 / build | The prior candidate instrument compiled both codecs into a global registry despite the draft registration status. How is installation registration determined? | Resolved by OWNER 2026-10-14, differential run 4, profile §8 Codec registry per installation: derive supplements solely from the installed catalog alg. Classical or unknown alg adds no supplement; the exact hybrid alg adds its pair codec to the baseline. A fallback installation treats both hybrid slots as opaque with cap 65536 and semantics give ALG_UNKNOWN. A hybrid installation retains classical rule O. This supersedes the previous compile-both reading; no bundle or source-code availability registers a codec. | "'`codec.py:BASELINE_CODECS`, `registered_codecs`; `verify.py:verify_bundle`; profile §8, lines 900–905; supplement §§1–3 |'"',
prototype/indep-verifier/codex-r4.log:13825:'A15': '| A15 | 3.1, 9.3 versus 5.x, 9.1–9.2, 9.4–9.5 | EA-31 says unsupported signatures and possession are not evaluated, while r2-F01 requires their own codecs and row 9.3 lists only presence as its prerequisite. | Interpret non-evaluation as semantic non-evaluation. Receipt and possession codecs still run within the installation registry, including codec-known unselected ids. Hybrid ids are opaque under fallback, while classical ids retain rule O under hybrid. Unsupported key parsing, fingerprint binding and signature/possession policy/math do not run. Codec-invalid bytes still contribute INVALID and independent schema/hash checks still run. | "'`verify.py:verify_bundle`; `codec.py:parse_signature`, `read_anchor`; profile §1 r2-F01, §8 EA-31 and Codec registry per installation, §15.7 rows 3.1/9.3 |'"',
prototype/indep-verifier/codex-r4.log:13826:'A18': '| A18 | 7.1, 8.3 / build | The draft/profile provides no actual frozen hybrid catalog bytes, hashes or new installation transport. Does support depend on bundled spec lookup or inferred registration? | Retain A02\\'s one-entry authenticated/provisioned catalog interface. Its alg selects support and the installation\\'s registered supplements independently of bundled spec hash lookup. A selected registered alg can still undergo semantics with SPEC_UNKNOWN. An unknown catalog alg registers no supplement and cannot manufacture support. The checked-in release remains unprovisioned; no real frozen catalog or dated registration is fabricated. | "'`policy.py:parse_catalog`; `build_release.py`; `codec.py:registered_codecs`; `verify.py:verify_bundle`; profile §8, §14.2; supplement §§1,9 |'"'
