The first concrete discrepancy is a 4,303-byte JSON number, `0e` followed by 4,301 nines. It is an accepted spelling of zero under the text, but `check.py` crashes on Python’s integer-conversion limit while the independent codec accepts it.

I also confirmed that hybrid-rule differences disappear when both decoders use the registered hybrid configuration. I won’t count the baseline-only default as a format defect. The registered suite passed: 106 golden vectors and 236 rejection vectors.
